{"adjusted_val_bpb": 0.36500806180760215, "attempt": 0, "charged": true, "critic": {"issues": ["No sign of gaming the measurement. The new code reads no files, contains no pasted answers and does not use the test labels. The kNN correction uses only train_y (through the in-sample residuals) and test_smiles, which fit_predict is allowed to use.", "Design weakness, not a veto: the residuals come from the same training data the boosted model was fitted on (y - (base_tr + stage2.predict(Xtr))). The model fits its own training data closely, so these residuals are small and do not reflect its errors on new molecules. The 0.3 * kNN-residual correction therefore does very little, which matches the negligible change in loss.", "The edit adds about 12 lines and refits Morgan bits that probably duplicate existing features, for a gain of 0.0005, which is far below the noise sd of 0.0037. Under the 'simpler is better' rule it should not be accepted.", "My z: (0.3655 - 0.365) / (0.0037 * sqrt(1/1 + 1/2)) \u2248 0.110. The harness reports 0.112; the small gap is probably because the displayed values are rounded. This agrees with the harness's provisional decision to reject.", "This is a single candidate run. A z of about 0.11 shows no evidence of improvement, and a replicate run is not worth a slot."], "ok": true, "veto": false}, "decision": "reject", "description": "Add a 0.3-shrunk Tanimoto k=5 nearest-neighbour correction using the final model's training residuals to the ridge + two-stage XGBoost prediction.", "edit_class": "structural", "flags": [], "gpu": "pine", "idea_id": "b015", "incumbent_after": {"mean": 0.3655190361773364, "n": 2}, "incumbent_before": {"mean": 0.3655190361773364, "n": 2}, "job_id": "B1_caco_HH_1_cs0-candidate-6_1795047374370", "kind": "candidate", "lint": {"hard": [], "ok": true, "warnings": []}, "model_calls": [{"cost_usd_nominal": 0.0312824, "cost_usd_plan": 0.0312824, "latency_s": 7.373109635023866, "requested_model": "sonnet", "role": "coder", "serv